// An `if` EXPRESSION with no `else`, at a SENTINEL-nullable scalar rep. `vl check` returns 0 and
// the emitter refuses with `emitProgram: if-expression requires an else arm`
// (`compiler/wasmEmit.vl:13116`, the `emitIfExprAs` site). Should print 1.
//
// THE REP PICKS THE SITE, and that is why this is a separate probe from
// `if-expr-no-else-string-arm.vl` rather than a second spelling of it. A `boolean` then-arm
// declines every rung of `ifExprRefKind` — not a closure, join kind is not 3, not string /
// array / map, `structIndexOfExpr` falls to its `-1` tail, not an ObjLit, and `boolean | null`
// is not a nullable struct — so `emitIfExpr` routes to `emitIfExprAs` and hits ITS guard.
//
// An `i32` then-arm reaches a THIRD site (`wasmEmit.vl:5502`, `union if-expression requires an
// else arm`) via the value-union box path, so the same missing `else` has at least three
// emit-side homes. Attribution here was settled with an instrumented compiler, not by reading.
const x = if true { true }
if x != null { print(1) }
